outputs.ts's ExitCodeOptions doc comment and runtime.ts's execute() implement the same invariant: no stdout is ever written on the stderr/BLOCK(2) exit path, because Claude Code's hook-result parser treats any stdout that parses as valid JSON as success regardless of exit code. SKILL.md and README document this contract for hook authors; if the implementation changes, both docs go stale with nothing else catching it.
